sisted witness inside the config transaction, reads the sequence ref, requires it to stand on or continue that witness, and independently checks the older verified head's ancestry and exact depth distance. A permitted stale read leaves the disk witness unchanged and adopts the newer stored witness into workspace memory; unreadable refs, rewound refs, off-history heads and dishonest distances fail closed. Strict attach remains safe under its existing rule. The documented limit is one observation of the ref at judgement time; an intervening rollback restored before that observation cannot be distinguished. No separate rollback bypass found in the changed read path. Current-head extension is only a liveness/continuation check; the returned data are still the older fully verified snapshot, and append retains its existing revalidation.\n\nSimplification: separate read judgement from the strict import guard is a clear design if the requester authorizes that scope. No need to duplicate the verifier or weaken the witness. Keep any correction narrow.\n\nValidation: independently ran go test -race ./internal/app -run 'Test(StaleVerification|StaleMemory|VerificationOff|AdmittedStale|ARefThatCannot|SnapshotInFlight|Attach|.*Frontier)' -count=1 -timeout 20m: pass (14.507s). Retained lane2-full-r2.log has 36 passing packages and exit=0; lane2-race-r2.log passes app/apphost at this head. Checked the two new mutation logs: removing continued-ref acceptance and relaxing exact distance turn their respective proofs red. Diff check passes and the checkout remains clean at the exact head. The read implementation and its current gates are not the blocker; the unfulfilled attach condition is.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:ceab593d2c0ddf591b486936d1c554ae386f7522","binding":"assigned","head":"afdb06a67795f9f1b0dd821e3540b42a5f8bfe41","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:ece5ad7835bafce14516